#       Multibyte text in regular files, for the counts that follow LC_CTYPE:
#       wc -m, -w and -L in a UTF-8 locale. A set of its own so no pinned row
#       of the text set moves. utf8.txt mixes two, three and four byte
#       characters, double-width ones, the no-break and wide spaces GNU splits
#       words at, and bytes that are no character; utf8_edge.txt ends its
#       first 65536 bytes inside a character, where a read does.
